<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q=5</annotation></semantics></math>, the independence polynomial of <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G\cong\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{45})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>45</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G\cong\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{45})</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
