<p id="S3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We give detailed information for this example. The set of vertices <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V(G)</annotation></semantics></math> can be partitioned based on the greatest common divisor of an element with <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 45." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 45.</annotation></semantics></math> Let <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{d}=\{v\in V\mid\gcd(v,45)=d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>gcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>45</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{d}=\{v\in V\mid\gcd(v,45)=d\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The possible values for <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d</annotation></semantics></math> are the divisors of <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>45</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 45</annotation></semantics></math> other than <math id="S3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 45," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 45,</annotation></semantics></math> which are <math id="S3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 3,5,9,15." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 3,5,9,15.</annotation></semantics></math> The sizes of the vertex partitions <math id="S3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> are as: <math id="S3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|V_{3}|=\varphi(45/3)=\varphi(15)=8,|V_{5}|=\varphi(45/5)=\varphi(9)=6,|V_{9}|=\varphi(45/9)=\varphi(5)=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>15</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|V_{3}|=\varphi(45/3)=\varphi(15)=8,|V_{5}|=\varphi(45/5)=\varphi(9)=6,|V_{9}|=\varphi(45/9)=\varphi(5)=4</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|V_{15}|=\varphi(45/15)=\varphi(3)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|V_{15}|=\varphi(45/15)=\varphi(3)=2</annotation></semantics></math>.
The order <math id="S3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|V|=8+6+4+2=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|V|=8+6+4+2=20</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, <math id="S3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{15}=\{15,30\},V_{5}=\{5,10,20,25,35,40\},V_{9}=\{9,18,27,36\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>36</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{15}=\{15,30\},V_{5}=\{5,10,20,25,35,40\},V_{9}=\{9,18,27,36\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{3}=\{3,6,12,21,24,33,39,42\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>39</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>42</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{3}=\{3,6,12,21,24,33,39,42\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
The sets <math id="S3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{3},V_{5},V_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{3},V_{5},V_{9}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent sets, and the set <math id="S3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{15}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{15}</annotation></semantics></math> induces a <math id="S3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Every vertex in <math id="S3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{15}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{15}</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to every vertex in <math id="S3.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{3}\cup V_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{3}\cup V_{9}</annotation></semantics></math>, and every vertex in <math id="S3.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to every vertex in <math id="S3.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{9}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{9}.</annotation></semantics></math> The graph <math id="S3.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G</annotation></semantics></math> is shown in Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 Independence polynomial of zero divisor graph of ℤ_{𝑝^2⁢𝑞} ‣ Combinatorial and analytic aspects of independence polynomials of zero divisor graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with green vertices in <math id="S3.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{15}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{15}</annotation></semantics></math>, blue in <math id="S3.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{9}</annotation></semantics></math>, and white in <math id="S3.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{5}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{5},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
