<p id="S3.p7.11" class="ltx_p">All coefficients in the above expansion are non-negative, and the constant term is positive. Therefore, <math id="S3.p7.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi(p,s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi(p,s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.p7.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(q-1)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(q-1)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that
<math id="S3.p7.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{2}^{2}-h_{1}h_{3}&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{2}^{2}-h_{1}h_{3}&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence
Thus
<math id="S3.p7.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{2}^{2}\geq h_{1}h_{3}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{2}^{2}\geq h_{1}h_{3}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Thus, it follows that <math id="S3.p7.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{p,q}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{p,q}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave. Finally, since <math id="S3.p7.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1+x)^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1+x)^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave and has no internal zeros, and <math id="S3.p7.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{p,q}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{p,q}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave with positive coefficients, so their product
<math id="S3.p7.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q});x)=(1+x)^{c}H_{p,q}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q});x)=(1+x)^{c}H_{p,q}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>
is log-concave. Hence, the coefficient sequence of <math id="S3.p7.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q});x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q});x)</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave. Moreover, all coefficients of <math id="S3.p7.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q});x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q});x)</annotation></semantics></math> are positive. A positive log-concave sequence has no internal zeros and is unimodal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>. Therefore, <math id="S3.p7.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q});x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q});x)</annotation></semantics></math> is unimodal.
 <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:5.7pt;height:5.7pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Clearly, <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x=-1</annotation></semantics></math> is a zero of the polynomial <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q}),x)</annotation></semantics></math>. For other zeros the independence polynomial of <math id="S3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q}),</annotation></semantics></math> we have the following result, which gives their annular region.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the independence polynomial of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math> are primes. Then all zeros of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(x)</annotation></semantics></math> different from <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x=-1</annotation></semantics></math> lie in the annular region</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{x\in\mathbb{C}:\frac{1}{2}&lt;|1+x|&lt;2\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{x\in\mathbb{C}:\frac{1}{2}&lt;|1+x|&lt;2\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
Since the independence polynomial of <math id="S3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q})</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(x)=(1+x)^{(p-1)(p+q-1)}+(1+x)^{p(q-1)}-(1+x)^{(p-1)(q-1)}+(p-1)x(1+x)^{p(p-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(x)=(1+x)^{(p-1)(p+q-1)}+(1+x)^{p(q-1)}-(1+x)^{(p-1)(q-1)}+(p-1)x(1+x)^{p(p-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.2" class="ltx_p">With
<math id="S3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y=1+x," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y=1+x,</annotation></semantics></math> the above polynomial becomes</p>
<table id="S3.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(y-1)=y^{(p-1)(p+q-1)}+y^{p(q-1)}-y^{(p-1)(q-1)}+(p-1)(y-1)y^{p(p-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(y-1)=y^{(p-1)(p+q-1)}+y^{p(q-1)}-y^{(p-1)(q-1)}+(p-1)(y-1)y^{p(p-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(p-1)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(p-1)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows immediately that <math id="S3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y=0</annotation></semantics></math>, that is <math id="S3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, is a zero of <math id="S3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. We are interested only in the other zeros, so we assume <math id="S3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. The polynomial can be written as <math id="S3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(y-1)=y^{p(p-1)}Q(y)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(y-1)=y^{p(p-1)}Q(y),</annotation></semantics></math>
where</p>
<table id="S3.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(y)=y^{A}+y^{B}-y^{C}+(p-1)y-(p-1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>B</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(y)=y^{A}+y^{B}-y^{C}+(p-1)y-(p-1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.4" class="ltx_p">with
<math id="S3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A=(p-1)(q-1),B=p(q-p)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A=(p-1)(q-1),B=p(q-p),</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C=(p-1)(q-p-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C=(p-1)(q-p-1).</annotation></semantics></math>
Thus the zeros of <math id="S3.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(x)</annotation></semantics></math> different from <math id="S3.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x=-1</annotation></semantics></math> correspond exactly to the non-zero zeros of <math id="S3.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. It is therefore enough to prove that every zero <math id="S3.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="S3.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;|y|&lt;2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;|y|&lt;2.</annotation></semantics></math>
We shall prove separately that <math id="S3.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|y|\leq\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|y|\leq\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and for <math id="S3.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|y|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|y|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
First suppose that <math id="S3.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|y|\leq\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|y|\leq\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we will show that <math id="S3.p9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="S3.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r=|y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r=|y|</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.p9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p-1)=y^{A}+y^{B}-y^{C}+(p-1)y." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>B</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p-1)=y^{A}+y^{B}-y^{C}+(p-1)y.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.5" class="ltx_p">Now, with absolute values, we have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p-1\leq r^{A}+r^{B}+r^{C}+(p-1)r." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p-1\leq r^{A}+r^{B}+r^{C}+(p-1)r.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.6" class="ltx_p">Next, we check that the right-hand side of above inequality is always strictly smaller than <math id="S3.p9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S3.p9.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(p,q)=(2,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(p,q)=(2,3)</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S3.p9.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=2y^{2}+y-2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=2y^{2}+y-2.</annotation></semantics></math>
If <math id="S3.p9.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|y|\leq\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|y|\leq\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2=|2y^{2}+y|\leq 2|y|^{2}+|y|\leq 2\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}+\frac{1}{2}=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2=|2y^{2}+y|\leq 2|y|^{2}+|y|\leq 2\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}+\frac{1}{2}=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.7" class="ltx_p">which is impossible. Next, let <math id="S3.p9.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="S3.p9.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=y^{q-1}+y^{2q-4}-y^{q-3}+y-1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=y^{q-1}+y^{2q-4}-y^{q-3}+y-1.</annotation></semantics></math>
If <math id="S3.p9.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S3.p9.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1\leq r^{q-1}+r^{2q-4}+r^{q-3}+r." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1\leq r^{q-1}+r^{2q-4}+r^{q-3}+r.</annotation></semantics></math>
Since <math id="S3.p9.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r\leq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r\leq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="S3.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{4}+\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{6}+\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}+\frac{1}{2}=\frac{53}{64}&lt;1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>53</mn><mn>64</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{4}+\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{6}+\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}+\frac{1}{2}=\frac{53}{64}&lt;1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.8" class="ltx_p">a contradiction. For <math id="S3.p9.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p=3</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S3.p9.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math> and both <math id="S3.p9.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q</annotation></semantics></math> are primes, so we have <math id="S3.p9.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=2(q-1)\geq 8,\qquad B=3(q-3)\geq 6,\qquad C=2(q-4)\geq 2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=2(q-1)\geq 8,\qquad B=3(q-3)\geq 6,\qquad C=2(q-4)\geq 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.9" class="ltx_p">Thus, if <math id="S3.p9.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|y|\leq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|y|\leq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{8}+\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{6}+\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}+2\cdot\frac{1}{2}&lt;2," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{8}+\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{6}+\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}+2\cdot\frac{1}{2}&lt;2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.10" class="ltx_p">which is again impossible. For <math id="S3.p9.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S3.p9.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q</annotation></semantics></math> are odd primes with <math id="S3.p9.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, so we have <math id="S3.p9.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q\geq p+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q\geq p+2</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,
<math id="S3.p9.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C=(p-1)(q-p-1)\geq p-1\geq 4." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C=(p-1)(q-p-1)\geq p-1\geq 4.</annotation></semantics></math>
Also <math id="S3.p9.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we derive</p>
<table id="S3.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{A}+r^{B}+r^{C}+(p-1)r\leq 3\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{4}+\frac{p-1}{2}=\frac{3}{16}+\frac{p-1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{A}+r^{B}+r^{C}+(p-1)r\leq 3\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{4}+\frac{p-1}{2}=\frac{3}{16}+\frac{p-1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.11" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.p9.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.p9.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p-1\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p-1\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>, and so
<math id="S3.p9.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{3}{16}+\frac{p-1}{2}&lt;p-1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{3}{16}+\frac{p-1}{2}&lt;p-1.</annotation></semantics></math>
This contradicts the inequality obtained from <math id="S3.p9.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S3.p9.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)</annotation></semantics></math> has no zeros in <math id="S3.p9.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|y|\leq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|y|\leq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to show that <math id="S3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)</annotation></semantics></math> has no zeros in <math id="S3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|y|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|y|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r=|y|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r=|y|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the relations
<math id="S3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A-C=p(p-1),B-C=q-1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A-C=p(p-1),B-C=q-1,</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="S3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A-B=p(p-1)-(q-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A-B=p(p-1)-(q-1).</annotation></semantics></math>
We have to consider three cases. If <math id="S3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A&gt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A&gt;B</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A-B\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A-B\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y^{A}=-y^{B}+y^{C}-(p-1)y+(p-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>B</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y^{A}=-y^{B}+y^{C}-(p-1)y+(p-1).</annotation></semantics></math>
With absolute values, we get</p>
<table id="S3.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq r^{B-A}+r^{C-A}+(p-1)r^{1-A}+(p-1)r^{-A}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq r^{B-A}+r^{C-A}+(p-1)r^{1-A}+(p-1)r^{-A}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A-C=p(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A-C=p(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, this implies that</p>
<table id="S3.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq 2^{-(A-B)}+2^{-p(p-1)}+(p-1)2^{-(A-1)}+(p-1)2^{-A}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq 2^{-(A-B)}+2^{-p(p-1)}+(p-1)2^{-(A-1)}+(p-1)2^{-A}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.3" class="ltx_p">For case <math id="S3.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A&gt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A&gt;B</annotation></semantics></math>, we necessarily have <math id="S3.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q\geq p+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q\geq p+2</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain
<math id="S3.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A=(p-1)(q-1)\geq(p-1)(p+1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A=(p-1)(q-1)\geq(p-1)(p+1),</annotation></semantics></math>
and hence <math id="S3.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A-1\geq p(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A-1\geq p(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we obtain</p>
<table id="S3.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq\frac{1}{2}+2^{-p(p-1)}+(p-1)2^{-p(p-1)}+(p-1)2^{-p(p-1)-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq\frac{1}{2}+2^{-p(p-1)}+(p-1)2^{-p(p-1)}+(p-1)2^{-p(p-1)-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.4" class="ltx_p">or equivalently,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1+\frac{3}{2}(p-1)}{2^{p(p-1)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1+\frac{3}{2}(p-1)}{2^{p(p-1)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.5" class="ltx_p">But <math id="S3.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S3.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(p-1)\geq 6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(p-1)\geq 6</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence</p>
<table id="S3.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1+\frac{3}{2}(p-1)}{2^{p(p-1)}}&lt;\frac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1+\frac{3}{2}(p-1)}{2^{p(p-1)}}&lt;\frac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.6" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the right-hand side is strictly less than <math id="S3.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction. Hence <math id="S3.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|y|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|y|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> in the case <math id="S3.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A&gt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A&gt;B</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now, for <math id="S3.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A=B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A=B</annotation></semantics></math>, we get
<math id="S3.p10.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=2y^{A}-y^{C}+(p-1)y-(p-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=2y^{A}-y^{C}+(p-1)y-(p-1).</annotation></semantics></math>
If <math id="S3.p10.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S3.p10.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2r^{A}\leq r^{C}+(p-1)r+(p-1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2r^{A}\leq r^{C}+(p-1)r+(p-1),</annotation></semantics></math> and thereby we have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq r^{C-A}+(p-1)r^{1-A}+(p-1)r^{-A}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq r^{C-A}+(p-1)r^{1-A}+(p-1)r^{-A}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.7" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.p10.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A-C=p(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A-C=p(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p10.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, the right-hand side of above inequality is at most</p>
<table id="S3.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{-p(p-1)}+(p-1)2^{1-A}+(p-1)2^{-A}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{-p(p-1)}+(p-1)2^{1-A}+(p-1)2^{-A},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.8" class="ltx_p">which is strictly less than <math id="S3.p10.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly, for <math id="S3.p10.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(p,q)=(2,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(p,q)=(2,3)</annotation></semantics></math>, it is at most
<math id="S3.p10.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1}{4}=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1}{4}=1,</annotation></semantics></math>
and for <math id="S3.p10.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> it is even smaller, since <math id="S3.p10.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p10.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math> are larger. Thus, we get a contradiction. Therefore <math id="S3.p10.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.p10.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|y|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|y|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> in the case <math id="S3.p10.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A=B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A=B</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, if <math id="S3.p10.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B&gt;A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B&gt;A</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S3.p10.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B-A=(q-1)-p(p-1)&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B-A=(q-1)-p(p-1)&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math>
Since <math id="S3.p10.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q</annotation></semantics></math> is odd and <math id="S3.p10.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math> is even, the positive integer <math id="S3.p10.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B-A</annotation></semantics></math> is in fact at least <math id="S3.p10.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.p10.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{B}=-y^{A}+y^{C}-(p-1)y+(p-1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>B</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{B}=-y^{A}+y^{C}-(p-1)y+(p-1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.9" class="ltx_p">and hence</p>
<table id="S3.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq r^{A-B}+r^{C-B}+(p-1)r^{1-B}+(p-1)r^{-B}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq r^{A-B}+r^{C-B}+(p-1)r^{1-B}+(p-1)r^{-B}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.10" class="ltx_p">With <math id="S3.p10.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B-C=q-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B-C=q-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="S3.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq 2^{-(B-A)}+2^{-(q-1)}+(p-1)2^{1-B}+(p-1)2^{-B}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq 2^{-(B-A)}+2^{-(q-1)}+(p-1)2^{1-B}+(p-1)2^{-B}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.11" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.p10.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B-A\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B-A\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p10.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q-1\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q-1\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>, the first two terms are bounded by <math id="S3.p10.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{4}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p10.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{16}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Also, we note that
<math id="S3.p10.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(p-1)2^{1-B}+(p-1)2^{-B}=\tfrac{3(p-1)}{2^{B}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>B</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(p-1)2^{1-B}+(p-1)2^{-B}=\tfrac{3(p-1)}{2^{B}}.</annotation></semantics></math>
If <math id="S3.p10.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p=2</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p10.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S3.p10.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B=2(q-2)\geq 6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B=2(q-2)\geq 6</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore
<math id="S3.p10.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{3(p-1)}{2^{B}}\leq\tfrac{3}{64}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>B</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>64</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{3(p-1)}{2^{B}}\leq\tfrac{3}{64}.</annotation></semantics></math>
If <math id="S3.p10.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p10.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B&gt;A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B&gt;A</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="S3.p10.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q-1&gt;p(p-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q-1&gt;p(p-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and so <math id="S3.p10.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B=p(q-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B=p(q-p)</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large. In particular,
<math id="S3.p10.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{3(p-1)}{2^{B}}&lt;\tfrac{1}{4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>B</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{3(p-1)}{2^{B}}&lt;\tfrac{1}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Thus, in all cases we get
<math id="S3.p10.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1&lt;\tfrac{1}{4}+\tfrac{1}{16}+\tfrac{1}{4}&lt;1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1&lt;\tfrac{1}{4}+\tfrac{1}{16}+\tfrac{1}{4}&lt;1,</annotation></semantics></math>
which is absurd. Therefore, <math id="S3.p10.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)</annotation></semantics></math> has no zeros with <math id="S3.p10.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|y|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|y|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> in the case <math id="S3.p10.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B&gt;A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B&gt;A</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, by combining the two parts, every zero <math id="S3.p10.m64" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.p10.m65" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="S3.p10.m66" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;|y|&lt;2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;|y|&lt;2.</annotation></semantics></math>
Since the zeros of <math id="S3.p10.m67" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(x)</annotation></semantics></math> different from <math id="S3.p10.m68" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x=-1</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to the zeros of <math id="S3.p10.m69" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(y)</annotation></semantics></math> under the change of variable <math id="S3.p10.m70" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y=1+x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y=1+x</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that every zero <math id="S3.p10.m71" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x\neq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x\neq-1</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.p10.m72" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(x)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="S3.p10.m73" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;|1+x|&lt;2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;|1+x|&lt;2.</annotation></semantics></math>
 <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:5.7pt;height:5.7pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q=5," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q=5,</annotation></semantics></math> the independent of <math id="S3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G\cong\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G\cong\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{p^{2}q})</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

