<p id="S3.p11.3" class="ltx_p">All the zeros of <math id="S3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(G,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(G,x)</annotation></semantics></math> are shown in (a) Figure <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3 Independence polynomial of zero divisor graph of ℤ_{𝑝^2⁢𝑞} ‣ Combinatorial and analytic aspects of independence polynomials of zero divisor graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The zeros of <math id="S3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(G,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(G,x)</annotation></semantics></math> other than <math id="S3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x=-1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x=-1,</annotation></semantics></math> are shown in (b) Figure <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3 Independence polynomial of zero divisor graph of ℤ_{𝑝^2⁢𝑞} ‣ Combinatorial and analytic aspects of independence polynomials of zero divisor graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, and clearly they lie in annular region <math id="S3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;|1+x|&lt;2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;|1+x|&lt;2.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
