</table>
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The independence polynomial <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(x)=\sum_{I\in\mathcal{I}}x^{|I|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(x)=\sum_{I\in\mathcal{I}}x^{|I|}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sum of the polynomials for each family. Let <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the polynomial for family <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the family <math id="S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, an independent set <math id="S4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\in\mathcal{I}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\in\mathcal{I}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a subset of <math id="S4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{q}\cup V_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{q}\cup V_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since there are no edges within or between these partitions, any subset of <math id="S4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{q}\cup V_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{q}\cup V_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is an independent set. Their cardinal number is <math id="S4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|+|V_{r}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|+|V_{r}|</annotation></semantics></math>, and the corresponding polynomial is</p>
<table id="S4.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{0}(x)=(1+x)^{|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|+|V_{r}|}=(1+x)^{(q-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(q-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{0}(x)=(1+x)^{|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|+|V_{r}|}=(1+x)^{(q-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(q-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">For the family <math id="S4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\in\mathcal{I}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\in\mathcal{I}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\cap V_{pq}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\cap V_{pq}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="S4.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\cap V_{pr}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\cap V_{pr}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\cap V_{qr}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\cap V_{qr}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. Due to the edges between <math id="S4.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, we must have <math id="S4.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\cap V_{r}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\cap V_{r}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S4.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I</annotation></semantics></math> must be a subset of <math id="S4.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{q}\cup V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{q}\cup V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. This union of sets induces a subgraph with no edges, so any of its subsets is an independent set. The condition for being in <math id="S4.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is that the subset must have a non-empty intersection with <math id="S4.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The generating function for all subsets of <math id="S4.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{q}\cup V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{q}\cup V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1+x)^{|V_{p}|}(1+x)^{|V_{q}|}(1+x)^{|V_{r}|}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1+x)^{|V_{p}|}(1+x)^{|V_{q}|}(1+x)^{|V_{r}|},</annotation></semantics></math> which is equivalent to
<math id="S4.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1+x)^{|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|+|V_{pq}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1+x)^{|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|+|V_{pq}|}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The generating function for subsets that do not intersect <math id="S4.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> (that is, subsets of <math id="S4.p3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>) is <math id="S4.p3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1+x)^{|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1+x)^{|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|}</annotation></semantics></math>.
So, we obtain</p>
<table id="S4.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}(x)=(1+x)^{|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|+|V_{pq}|}-(1+x)^{|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}(x)=(1+x)^{|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|+|V_{pq}|}-(1+x)^{|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Now, with the values</p>
<table id="S4.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|+|V_{pq}|=(r-1)(q-1+p-1+1)=(r-1)(p+q-1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|+|V_{pq}|=(r-1)(q-1+p-1+1)=(r-1)(p+q-1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.5" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S4.p3.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|=(q-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(r-1)=(r-1)(p+q-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|V_{p}|+|V_{q}|=(q-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(r-1)=(r-1)(p+q-2)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have</p>
<table id="S4.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}(x)=(1+x)^{(r-1)(p+q-1)}-(1+x)^{(r-1)(p+q-2)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}(x)=(1+x)^{(r-1)(p+q-1)}-(1+x)^{(r-1)(p+q-2)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Again for the family <math id="S4.p3.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.p3.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\in\mathcal{I}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\in\mathcal{I}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p3.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\cap V_{pr}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\cap V_{pr}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="S4.p3.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\cap V_{q}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\cap V_{q}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. So, <math id="S4.p3.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I</annotation></semantics></math> is a subset of <math id="S4.p3.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{r}\cup V_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{p}\cup V_{r}\cup V_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.p3.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\cap V_{pr}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\cap V_{pr}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. With the similar idea as above we have</p>
<table id="S4.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V_{p}|+|V_{r}|+|V_{pr}|=(q-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(q-1)+(q-1)=(q-1)(p+r-1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V_{p}|+|V_{r}|+|V_{pr}|=(q-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(q-1)+(q-1)=(q-1)(p+r-1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.7" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S4.p3.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|V_{p}|+|V_{r}|=(q-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(q-1)=(q-1)(p+r-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|V_{p}|+|V_{r}|=(q-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(q-1)=(q-1)(p+r-2)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, with these values, we have</p>
<table id="S4.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}(x)=(1+x)^{(q-1)(p+r-1)}-(1+x)^{(q-1)(p+r-2)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}(x)=(1+x)^{(q-1)(p+r-1)}-(1+x)^{(q-1)(p+r-2)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.8" class="ltx_p">Finally for the family <math id="S4.p3.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.p3.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\in\mathcal{I}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\in\mathcal{I}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p3.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\cap V_{qr}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\cap V_{qr}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="S4.p3.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\cap V_{p}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\cap V_{p}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. So, <math id="S4.p3.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I</annotation></semantics></math> is a subset of <math id="S4.p3.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{q}\cup V_{r}\cup V_{qr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{q}\cup V_{r}\cup V_{qr}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.p3.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\cap V_{qr}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\cap V_{qr}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the size of sets are
<math id="S4.p3.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|V_{q}|+|V_{r}|+|V_{qr}|=(p-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(q-1)+(p-1)=(p-1)(q+r-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|V_{q}|+|V_{r}|+|V_{qr}|=(p-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(q-1)+(p-1)=(p-1)(q+r-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p3.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|V_{q}|+|V_{r}|=(p-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(q-1)=(p-1)(q+r-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|V_{q}|+|V_{r}|=(p-1)(r-1)+(p-1)(q-1)=(p-1)(q+r-2)</annotation></semantics></math>. The generating function is</p>
<table id="S4.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{3}(x)=(1+x)^{(p-1)(q+r-1)}-(1+x)^{(p-1)(q+r-2)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{3}(x)=(1+x)^{(p-1)(q+r-1)}-(1+x)^{(p-1)(q+r-2)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.9" class="ltx_p">The total independence polynomial <math id="S4.p3.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.p3.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.p3.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)=I_{0}(x)+I_{1}(x)+I_{2}(x)+I_{3}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)=I_{0}(x)+I_{1}(x)+I_{2}(x)+I_{3}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting the expressions and sizes gives the final expression as in statement.
 <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:5.7pt;height:5.7pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we discuss the zeros of the polynomial <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> in plane and illustrate result with an example.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the independence polynomial of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p&lt;q&lt;r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p&lt;q&lt;r</annotation></semantics></math> are primes. Then <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x=-1</annotation></semantics></math> is a zero of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> with multiplicity <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(p-1)(q+r-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(p-1)(q+r-2)</annotation></semantics></math>, and every other zero <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;|1+x|&lt;2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;|1+x|&lt;2.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
We use compact notations with
<math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a=p-1,b=q-1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a=p-1,b=q-1,</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c=r-1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c=r-1.</annotation></semantics></math> So, it is clear that <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1\leq a&lt;b&lt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1\leq a&lt;b&lt;c</annotation></semantics></math>. In the independence polynomial of <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr})</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="S4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y=1+x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y=1+x</annotation></semantics></math>, and obtain</p>
<table id="S4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle I(y-1)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle I(y-1)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex101.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle\,y^{ab+bc+ca}+y^{ab+ac+a}-y^{ab+ac}+y^{ab+bc+b}-y^{ab+bc}+y^{ac+bc+c}-y^{ac+bc}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle\,y^{ab+bc+ca}+y^{ab+ac+a}-y^{ab+ac}+y^{ab+bc+b}-y^{ab+bc}+y^{ac+bc+c}-y^{ac+bc}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
