<p id="S4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a&lt;b&lt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a&lt;b&lt;c</annotation></semantics></math>, the smallest exponent appearing in this expression is <math id="S4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle ab+ac=a(b+c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle ab+ac=a(b+c)</annotation></semantics></math>, and its coefficient is <math id="S4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y=0</annotation></semantics></math> is a zero of <math id="S4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(y-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(y-1)</annotation></semantics></math> with multiplicity <math id="S4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a(b+c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a(b+c)</annotation></semantics></math>, and thereby <math id="S4.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x=-1</annotation></semantics></math> is a zero of <math id="S4.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(x)</annotation></semantics></math> with multiplicity
<math id="S4.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a(b+c)=(p-1)(q+r-2)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a(b+c)=(p-1)(q+r-2).</annotation></semantics></math>We can put <math id="S4.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(y-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(y-1)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S4.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(y-1)=y^{ab+ac}H(y)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(y-1)=y^{ab+ac}H(y),</annotation></semantics></math>
where</p>
