<p id="S4.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Next, we we establish clear inequalities within above pairs of terms. Consider <math id="S4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{1}-A_{2}=(xy+xz+x)-(xy+xz)=x=p-1&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{1}-A_{2}=(xy+xz+x)-(xy+xz)=x=p-1&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math> it implies that <math id="S4.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{1}&gt;A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{1}&gt;A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, <math id="S4.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1}-C_{2}=(xy+yz+y)-(xy+yz)=y=q-1&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1}-C_{2}=(xy+yz+y)-(xy+yz)=y=q-1&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="S4.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1}&gt;C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1}&gt;C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}-D_{2}=(xz+yz+z)-(xz+yz)=z=r-1&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}-D_{2}=(xz+yz+z)-(xz+yz)=z=r-1&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="S4.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}&gt;D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}&gt;D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, we look for minimum among <math id="S4.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{A,A_{2},C_{2},D_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{A,A_{2},C_{2},D_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider <math id="S4.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{2}-A_{2}=(xy+yz)-(xy+xz)=yz-xz=z(y-x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{2}-A_{2}=(xy+yz)-(xy+xz)=yz-xz=z(y-x)</annotation></semantics></math>, then we get <math id="S4.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{2}&gt;A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{2}&gt;A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="S4.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y&gt;x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y&gt;x</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, <math id="S4.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{2}-C_{2}=(xz+yz)-(xy+yz)=xz-xy=x(z-y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{2}-C_{2}=(xz+yz)-(xy+yz)=xz-xy=x(z-y)</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="S4.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{2}&gt;C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{2}&gt;C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S4.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z&gt;y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z&gt;y</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S4.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{2}&lt;C_{2}&lt;D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{2}&lt;C_{2}&lt;D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, <math id="S4.p8.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A-A_{2}=(xy+yz+zx)-(xy+xz)=yz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A-A_{2}=(xy+yz+zx)-(xy+xz)=yz</annotation></semantics></math> gives us <math id="S4.p8.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A&gt;A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A&gt;A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="S4.p8.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y,z&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y,z&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, from these comparisons, <math id="S4.p8.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{2}=(p-1)(q+r-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{2}=(p-1)(q+r-2)</annotation></semantics></math> is the smallest among <math id="S4.p8.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{A,A_{2},C_{2},D_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{A,A_{2},C_{2},D_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, we search for the maximum exponent among <math id="S4.p8.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{A,A_{1},C_{1},D_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{A,A_{1},C_{1},D_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="S4.p8.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1}-A_{1}=(xy+yz+y)-(xy+xz+x)=yz-xz+y-x=z(y-x)+(y-x)=(z+1)(y-x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1}-A_{1}=(xy+yz+y)-(xy+xz+x)=yz-xz+y-x=z(y-x)+(y-x)=(z+1)(y-x)</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="S4.p8.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1}&gt;A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1}&gt;A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, as<math id="S4.p8.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z&gt;0,y&gt;x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z&gt;0,y&gt;x</annotation></semantics></math>. Again from
<math id="S4.p8.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}-C_{1}=(xz+yz+z)-(xy+yz+y)=xz-xy+z-y=x(z-y)+(z-y)=(x+1)(z-y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}-C_{1}=(xz+yz+z)-(xy+yz+y)=xz-xy+z-y=x(z-y)+(z-y)=(x+1)(z-y)</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="S4.p8.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}&gt;C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}&gt;C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S4.p8.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x&gt;0,z&gt;y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x&gt;0,z&gt;y</annotation></semantics></math>. So, we get ordering <math id="S4.p8.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{1}&lt;C_{1}&lt;D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{1}&lt;C_{1}&lt;D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now compare <math id="S4.p8.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.p8.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S4.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

