<p id="S4.p8.3" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.p8.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p8.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A-C_{1}=(r-1)-(q-1)=r-q&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A-C_{1}=(r-1)-(q-1)=r-q&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.p8.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p8.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p,q,r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p,q,r</annotation></semantics></math> are odd primes, so <math id="S4.p8.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q\geq p+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q\geq p+2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p8.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r\geq q+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r\geq q+2</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
