<p id="S4.p8.4" class="ltx_p">As <math id="S4.p8.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p8.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p-2\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p-2\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.p8.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(p-2)+p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(p-2)+p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and from above we get <math id="S4.p8.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A&gt;C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A&gt;C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is valid for all primes <math id="S4.p8.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p,q,r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p,q,r</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the maximum exponent is either <math id="S4.p8.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.p8.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, we compare them, and find the maximum exponent. With <math id="S4.p8.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}-A=(xz+yz+z)-(xy+yz+zx)=z-xy=(r-1)-(p-1)(q-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}-A=(xz+yz+z)-(xy+yz+zx)=z-xy=(r-1)-(p-1)(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that the sign of this difference is not constant, and depends on the specific values of <math id="S4.p8.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p,q,r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p,q,r</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.p8.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p=2</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p8.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}-A=(r-1)-(2-1)(q-1)=r-1-q+1=r-q&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}-A=(r-1)-(2-1)(q-1)=r-1-q+1=r-q&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. So, in this case, <math id="S4.p8.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is always greater than <math id="S4.p8.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.p8.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, then the sign of <math id="S4.p8.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}-A</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the sign of <math id="S4.p8.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(r-1)-(p-1)(q-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(r-1)-(p-1)(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.p8.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r\geq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r\geq 11</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p8.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(r-1)-(p-1)(q-1)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(r-1)-(p-1)(q-1)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and it follows that <math id="S4.p8.m64" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}&gt;A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}&gt;A</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the maximum element is not represented by a single expression for all primes <math id="S4.p8.m65" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p&lt;q&lt;r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p&lt;q&lt;r</annotation></semantics></math>. The maximum is <math id="S4.p8.m66" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S4.p8.m67" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(r-1)&gt;(p-1)(q-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(r-1)&gt;(p-1)(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p8.m68" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S4.p8.m69" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(r-1)&lt;(p-1)(q-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(r-1)&lt;(p-1)(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
 <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:5.7pt;height:5.7pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The minimum <math id="S4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r</annotation></semantics></math> among the coefficients of <math id="S4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r=pq+qr+pr-(p+q+r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r=pq+qr+pr-(p+q+r)</annotation></semantics></math>, since the coefficient of linear term in <math id="S4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex123.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle((p-1)(q+r-2))+(p-1)(q+r-1)-(r-1)(p+q-2)-(q-1)(p+r-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle((p-1)(q+r-2))+(p-1)(q+r-1)-(r-1)(p+q-2)-(q-1)(p+r-2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle+(r-1)(p+q-1)+(q-1)(p+r-1)-2(p+q+r)+pq+pr+qr+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle+(r-1)(p+q-1)+(q-1)(p+r-1)-2(p+q+r)+pq+pr+qr+3</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle=pq+qr+pr-(p+q+r)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle=pq+qr+pr-(p+q+r).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p9.2" class="ltx_p">By applying the Eneström-Kakeya theorem to <math id="S4.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x),</annotation></semantics></math> we have the following result.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The zeros of the polynomial <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(x)</annotation></semantics></math> lie in the annulus region</p>
<table id="S4.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{pq+qr+pr-(p+q+r)}\leq|Z|\leq R," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{pq+qr+pr-(p+q+r)}\leq|Z|\leq R,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R</annotation></semantics></math> is given as:</p>
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p=2</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R=(r-1)(p+q-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R=(r-1)(p+q-1).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R=(r-1)(p+q-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R=(r-1)(p+q-1)</annotation></semantics></math> provided <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r-1&gt;(p-1)(q-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r-1&gt;(p-1)(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R=pq+qr+pr-2(p+q+r)+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R=pq+qr+pr-2(p+q+r)+3</annotation></semantics></math> provided <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r-1&lt;(p-1)(q-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r-1&lt;(p-1)(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(x)=I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(x)=I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the independence polynomial of zero divisor graph <math id="S4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}).</annotation></semantics></math> Now, with <math id="S4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p=2,q=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p=2,q=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 5=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 5=5</annotation></semantics></math>, by Eneström-Kakeya theorem, the zeros of <math id="S4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(x)</annotation></semantics></math> lie in the annular region <math id="S4.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{21}\leq|x|\leq 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>21</mn></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{21}\leq|x|\leq 16</annotation></semantics></math>, which is much bigger region as compared to one given in Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4 Independence polynomial of zero divisor graph of order 𝑝⁢𝑞⁢𝑟 ‣ Combinatorial and analytic aspects of independence polynomials of zero divisor graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. Thus, Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4 Independence polynomial of zero divisor graph of order 𝑝⁢𝑞⁢𝑟 ‣ Combinatorial and analytic aspects of independence polynomials of zero divisor graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> gives better bounds as compared to Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4 Independence polynomial of zero divisor graph of order 𝑝⁢𝑞⁢𝑟 ‣ Combinatorial and analytic aspects of independence polynomials of zero divisor graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">As the coefficients of <math id="S4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> are positive, and it is known that a positive log-concave sequence is unimodal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>. So, if we prove log-concavity of <math id="S4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x),</annotation></semantics></math> then the unimodal proper will follow. Also, each each binomial term in <math id="S4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave due to symmetric behaviour of binomial coefficients. However sum of two log-concave polynomial is not necessarily log-concave. But due to symmetric behaviour of binomial terms in <math id="S4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x),</annotation></semantics></math> it looks like polynomial is log-concave and thereby unimodal. We leave it as a problem.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproblem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_problem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproblem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem 1</span></span><span id="Thmproblem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproblem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproblem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproblem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproblem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the independence polynomial of <math id="Thmproblem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr})</annotation></semantics></math>, with primes <math id="Thmproblem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p&lt;q&lt;r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p&lt;q&lt;r</annotation></semantics></math>. Then prove that <math id="Thmproblem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{pqr}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> is a unimodal and log-concave polynomial.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This article examines the independence polynomial <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n},x)</annotation></semantics></math> of the zero divisor graph <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> of commutative rings <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{Z}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{Z}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n\in\{p,p^{2},p^{3},pq,p^{2}q,pqr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n\in\{p,p^{2},p^{3},pq,p^{2}q,pqr\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p&lt;q&lt;r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p&lt;q&lt;r</annotation></semantics></math> are prime integers. The unimodal and log-concave properties of the previously stated graphs are analyzed. The positions of the zeros <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n}),x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n}),x)</annotation></semantics></math> in the plane are delineated, supplemented by pictures obtained from numerical computations. The independence polynomial’s application can be broadened to further values of <math id="S5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n</annotation></semantics></math> in the graph <math id="S5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varGamma(\mathbb{Z}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, and its components may be explored in subsequent research.</p>
</div>
</section>
